      "caveats": "The performance and convergence advantages of the controller were evaluated exclusively within a simulation environment rather than through real-world deployment.",
      "what": "The study develops a multi-objective adaptive traffic signal controller that decouples vehicle and pedestrian movements using an option-action reinforcement learning framework. It implements a linear scalarization mechanism to balance pedestrian and vehicle efficiency under varying weight preferences, alongside a value function approximation method that aggregates movement-level Q-values into phase-level estimates using a conflict matrix.",
